 "text": "..title\nA resolution authorizing The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County to abandon existing public water main, and to accept new public water main and new sanitary sewer manhole, for two properties located at 15 and 17 Music Circle South, also known as BBOP (MWS Project Nos. 26-WL-100 and 26-SL-129 and Proposal No. 2026M-085ES-001).\n..body\nWHEREAS, the abandonment of approximately 272 linear feet of existing six-inch water main, and the acceptance of approximately 272 linear feet of new eight-inch water main (DIP) and one new sanitary sewer manhole, for two properties located at 15 and 17 Music Circle South, also known as BBOP, are needed to construct project numbers 26-WL-100 and 26-SL-129; and,\nWHEREAS, BL2024-345 authorizes the Metropolitan Department of Water and Sewerage Services to approve extensions, additions, improvement, or works by resolution of the Metropolitan Council; and,\nWHEREAS, the Metropolitan Planning Commission approved mandatory referral No. 2026M085ES-001 on August 27, 2026, for the abandonment and acceptance of said water mains and sanitary sewer manhole.\nNOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE COUNCIL OF THE METROPOLITAN GOVERNMENT OF NASHVILLE AND DAVIDSON COUNTY:\nSection 1.\tThe Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County is authorized to abandon approximately 272 linear feet of existing six-inch water main, and to accept approximately 272 linear feet of new eight-inch water main (DIP) and one new sanitary sewer manhole, for two properties located at 15 and 17 Music Circle South, also known as BBOP, as shown on Exhibit 1, which is attached hereto and incorporated by reference.\nMap & Parcel: \t\t\t\tAddress:\n09313033100\t\t\t\t\t15 Music Circle South\n09313033200\t\t\t\t\t17 Music Circle South\nSection 2.\tThe Directors of Water and Sewerage Services and Public Property Administration are authorized to execute such documents as may be necessary and appropriate to carry out the abandonment and acceptance authorized by this resolution. \nSection 3.\tThis resolution shall take effect from and after its final passage, the welfare of The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County requiring it. \n..Agenda Analysis\nAnalysis\n\nThis resolution abandons approximately 272 linear feet of existing six-inch water main and accepts approximately 272 linear feet of new eight-inch water main (DIP) and one new sanitary sewer manhole, for two properties located at 15 and 17 Music Circle South, also known as BBOP.\n\nTennessee Code Annotated section 7-35-406(A)(2) and Ordinance No. BL2024-345 allow the Metropolitan Department of Water and Sewerage Services to approve extension, additions, or works by resolution of the Metropolitan Council.\n\nThis resolution has been approved by the Planning Commission.\n\n"
}
